
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Trickster has <a href="https://tricksterapp.com/">reached version 4.0</a>. I’ve used this app for years and I’m really impressed with the new version.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you haven&#8217;t tried it, Trickster lives in your Mac&#8217;s menu bar and keeps recently used files within reach. You can drag a file straight into an email or upload form without going back through the Finder.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The big addition in 4.0 is web links alongside those files. Extensions for Safari, Chrome, and Firefox let you send pages to Trickster, and optional automatic tracking can pick up supported cloud documents. Project filters can now collect local files and web links in the same view. That makes sense for work that lives partly on your Mac and partly in a browser.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The update also brings a Liquid Glass redesign and custom filter icons. It requires macOS Tahoe or later, so check that before upgrading.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Trickster 4 is a free update for existing owners. For new users, <a href="https://tricksterapp.com/press/">the full version is $29.99 as a one-time purchase</a>, with a 14-day trial available.</p>
